# Keep the build context lean.

# RUNTIME DATA IS NEVER PART OF AN IMAGE. It is bind-mounted at /app/data, so
# copying it in only makes the image enormous and the copy stale: `runs/` alone
# was 20 GB, and both the backend and scheduler images weighed 39.7 GB because
# of it. Nothing in the image reads these — every process reads the mount.
data/
.zevo-private/

# The same directories under their pre-consolidation names, so a checkout that
# still has them (or an older branch) does not quietly put them back.
runs/
workspace/
user_data/

.git

# Tests and project documentation are not read by an image.
tests/
docs/

# NOTE THE `**/`. A bare `__pycache__` matches only a top-level entry, so
# without it 113 stale .pyc files from tests/, ops/ and alembic/ were being
# baked into the image -- compiled against whatever the host's Python was,
# and shadowing nothing useful since the container recompiles anyway.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
.venv
venv
env
**/node_modules
web/dist
web/.vite
.env
.env.local
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
/tmp
